 106:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** 
 107:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** /** @defgroup HAL_Exported_Functions_Group1 Initialization and de-initialization Functions 
 108:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  *  @brief    Initialization and de-initialization functions
 109:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  *
 110:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** @verbatim    
 111:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  ===============================================================================
 112:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****               ##### Initialization and Configuration functions #####
 113:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  ===============================================================================
 114:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****     [..]  This section provides functions allowing to:
 115:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****       (+) Initializes the Flash interface the NVIC allocation and initial clock 
 116:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****           configuration. It initializes the systick also when timeout is needed 
 117:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****           and the backup domain when enabled.
 118:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****       (+) De-Initializes common part of the HAL.
 119:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****       (+) Configure the time base source to have 1ms time base with a dedicated 
 120:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****           Tick interrupt priority. 
 121:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****         (++) SysTick timer is used by default as source of time base, but user
 122:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              can eventually implement his proper time base source (a general purpose 
 123:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              timer for example or other time source), keeping in mind that Time base 
 124:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              duration should be kept 1ms since PPP_TIMEOUT_VALUEs are defined and 
 125:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              handled in milliseconds basis.
 126:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****         (++) Time base configuration function (HAL_InitTick ()) is called automatically 
 127:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              at the beginning of the program after reset by HAL_Init() or at any time 
 128:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              when clock is configured, by HAL_RCC_ClockConfig(). 
 129:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****         (++) Source of time base is configured  to generate interrupts at regular 
 130:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              time intervals. Care must be taken if HAL_Delay() is called from a 
 131:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              peripheral ISR process, the Tick interrupt line must have higher priority 
 132:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****             (numerically lower) than the peripheral interrupt. Otherwise the caller 
 133:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****             ISR process will be blocked. 
 134:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****        (++) functions affecting time base configurations are declared as __weak  
 135:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              to make  override possible  in case of other  implementations in user file.
 136:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** @endverbatim
 137:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   * @{
 138:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   */
 139:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** 
 140:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** /**
 141:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   * @brief  This function is used to initialize the HAL Library; it must be the first 
 142:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *         instruction to be executed in the main program (before to call any other
 143:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *         HAL function), it performs the following:
 144:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Configure the Flash prefetch, instruction and Data caches.
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccAKg4WO.s 			page 4


 145:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Configures the SysTick to generate an interrupt each 1 millisecond,
 146:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           which is clocked by the HSI (at this stage, the clock is not yet
 147:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           configured and thus the system is running from the internal HSI at 16 MHz).
 148:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Set NVIC Group Priority to 4.
 149:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Calls the HAL_MspInit() callback function defined in user file 
 150:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           "stm32f4xx_hal_msp.c" to do the global low level hardware initialization 
 151:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *            
 152:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   * @note   SysTick is used as time base for the HAL_Delay() function, the application
 153:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *         need to ensure that the SysTick time base is always set to 1 millisecond
